/-!
# Minimal primes of a ring carrying a composition law

Let `left`, `right`, `comp : A →+* C` be three ring maps and suppose that contracting a minimal
prime of `C` along `left` and along `right` sets up a bijection between the minimal primes of
`C` and the *pairs* of minimal primes of `A`.  If `comp` is flat and the contraction of a
minimal prime of `C` along `comp` contains its contractions along `left` and along `right`, then
`A` has a unique minimal prime.

This is the closing move of the proof of [Stacks Project, Tag 06E4]: there `A` is the étale
local ring of the arrow space `R` of a groupoid on a field at the identity `e`, `C` is the étale
local ring of `R ×_{s, U, t} R` at `(e, e)`, the three maps are the two projections and the
composition law, the bijection is Tag 06DU, and flatness of the composition law is Tag 06E0.

## Main results

* `StacksDraft.existsUnique_minimalPrimes_of_bijOn_comap_pair`: the bijection, the flatness and
  the two containments force `A` to have exactly one minimal prime.
* `StacksDraft.existsUnique_minimalPrimes_of_retraction_of_bijOn_comap_pair`: the same
  conclusion from the two retractions carried by the identity sections, in place of the two
  containments.
* `StacksDraft.comap_mem_minimalPrimes_of_flat_ringHom`: going down for minimal primes along a
  flat ring map, in the bare `RingHom` spelling.
* `StacksDraft.existsUnique_minimalPrimes_of_compositionLaw_strictHenselization`: the local
  computation of Tag 06E4, with the bijection and the smallest-prime refinement both supplied
  by Tag 06DU.
* `StacksDraft.existsUnique_minimalPrimes_of_compositionLaw_indEtale_base`: the same with the
  henselization hypothesis moved to the localized tensor square of an ind-étale base, which is
  the form an étale chart of an algebraic space provides.

## Implementation notes

The first form assumes nothing local: the argument needs only that `A` is nontrivial, so that it
has a minimal prime at all, and the two containments for the single minimal prime of `C`
obtained from the pair being compared.

Those two containments are hypotheses rather than consequences there.  The source deduces them
from two displayed commuting squares, but those squares as displayed say that the canonical map
`A ⊗_k A → C` factors as `comp` after `1 ⊗ e^#`, which would force `left = comp`; that fails
already for the additive group of the affine line, where `comp` sends the coordinate to
`x₁ + x₂` and `left` sends it to `x₁`.  What does hold is the dual statement for the section
`j₁ : R → R ×_{s, U, t} R`, `a ↦ (a, e)`: the induced `j₁^# : C → A` satisfies
`j₁^# ∘ comp = id`, `j₁^# ∘ left = id`, and `j₁^# ∘ right` is the structure map of `A` after
evaluation at the identity, so it kills the maximal ideal.  The second form takes exactly those
relations, for the two sections `a ↦ (a, e)` and `a ↦ (e, a)`, and derives the comparison of
`comp` with both members of the pair — in the opposite direction to the first form, which is
just as good because two minimal primes comparable either way are equal.

That derivation needs one piece of information about the bijection of Tag 06DU beyond
bijectivity: that the minimal prime of `C` matching a pair `(𝔭, 𝔭')` is the *smallest* prime of
`C` containing the images of `𝔭` and of `𝔭'`.  The two general forms carry it as the hypothesis
`hsmallest`; for the bijection of Tag 06DU itself it holds, because a minimal prime of `C` is
generated by the images of its two contractions
(`minimalPrimes_localized_tensorProduct_eq_sup`), and the last two theorems below discharge it
on that ground.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 06E4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06E4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06DU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06DU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06E0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06E0)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v

open scoped TensorProduct

namespace StacksDraft

/-- **Going down for minimal primes.** The contraction of a minimal prime along a flat ring map
is a minimal prime. -/
@[ega "IV 4.7.2" "more general"]
theorem comap_mem_minimalPrimes_of_flat_ringHom {A C : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing C]
    (f : A →+* C) (hf : f.Flat) {q : Ideal C} (hq : q ∈ minimalPrimes C) :
    q.comap f ∈ minimalPrimes A := by
  have : q.IsPrime := hq.1.1
  let : Algebra A C := f.toAlgebra
  have : Module.Flat A C := hf
  have : Algebra.HasGoingDown A C := Algebra.HasGoingDown.of_flat
  show q.comap (algebraMap A C) ∈ minimalPrimes A
  have hcp : (q.comap (algebraMap A C)).IsPrime := Ideal.comap_isPrime _ _
  refine ⟨⟨hcp, bot_le⟩, ?_⟩
  rintro P ⟨hP, -⟩ hPq
  have : q.LiesOver (q.comap (algebraMap A C)) := ⟨rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨P', hP'q, hP', hP'P⟩ := Ideal.exists_ideal_le_liesOver_of_le (p := P) q hPq
  exact (Ideal.comap_mono (hq.2 ⟨hP', bot_le⟩ hP'q)).trans (le_of_eq hP'P.over.symm)

/-- Of two minimal primes, one contained in the other, each is the other. -/
theorem eq_of_mem_minimalPrimes_of_le {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {p p' : Ideal A}
    (hp : p ∈ minimalPrimes A) (hp' : p' ∈ minimalPrimes A) (h : p ≤ p') : p = p' :=
  le_antisymm h (hp'.2 ⟨hp.1.1, bot_le⟩ h)

/-- If `comap comp q` is comparable with both `comap left q` and `comap right q` for all minimal
primes `q` of `C`, the bijection and flatness force a unique minimal prime of `A`. -/
private theorem existsUnique_minimalPrimes_of_comap_comparable {A C : Type u} [CommRing A]
    [Nontrivial A] [CommRing C] (left right comp : A →+* C)
    (hbij : Set.BijOn (fun q : Ideal C => (q.comap left, q.comap right))
      (minimalPrimes C) (minimalPrimes A ×ˢ minimalPrimes A))
    (hflat : comp.Flat)
    (hleft : ∀ q ∈ minimalPrimes C, q.comap left ≤ q.comap comp ∨ q.comap comp ≤ q.comap left)
    (hright : ∀ q ∈ minimalPrimes C,
      q.comap right ≤ q.comap comp ∨ q.comap comp ≤ q.comap right) :
    ∃! p : Ideal A, p ∈ minimalPrimes A := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := Ideal.exists_maximal A
  have : m.IsPrime := hm.isPrime
  obtain ⟨p₁, hp₁, -⟩ := Ideal.exists_minimalPrimes_le (I := (⊥ : Ideal A)) (J := m) bot_le
  have hp₀ : p₁ ∈ minimalPrimes A := hp₁
  refine ⟨p₁, hp₀, fun p hp => ?_⟩
  have hmem : ((p, p₁) : Ideal A × Ideal A) ∈ minimalPrimes A ×ˢ minimalPrimes A := ⟨hp, hp₀⟩
  obtain ⟨q, hq, hqeq⟩ := hbij.surjOn hmem
  simp only [Prod.mk.injEq] at hqeq
  obtain ⟨hq₁, hq₂⟩ := hqeq
  have hmin : q.comap comp ∈ minimalPrimes A :=
    comap_mem_minimalPrimes_of_flat_ringHom comp hflat hq
  have key : ∀ p' ∈ minimalPrimes A, p' ≤ q.comap comp ∨ q.comap comp ≤ p' →
      p' = q.comap comp := fun p' hp' h =>
    h.elim (eq_of_mem_minimalPrimes_of_le hp' hmin)
      fun h => (eq_of_mem_minimalPrimes_of_le hmin hp' h).symm
  exact (key p hp (by rw [← hq₁]; exact hleft q hq)).trans
    (key p₁ hp₀ (by rw [← hq₂]; exact hright q hq)).symm

/-- **The closing move of Stacks 06E4.** Let `left`, `right`, `comp : A →+* C` be ring maps such
that contracting along `left` and along `right` is a bijection from the minimal primes of `C` to
the pairs of minimal primes of `A`.  If `comp` is flat, and the contraction of a minimal prime of
`C` along `comp` contains its contractions along `left` and along `right`, then `A` has a unique
minimal prime.

Given minimal primes `p` and `p'` of `A`, surjectivity produces a minimal prime `q` of `C`
contracting to `p` along `left` and to `p'` along `right`.  Its contraction along `comp` is a
minimal prime of `A` by going down, and it contains both `p` and `p'`, so it equals both. -/
theorem existsUnique_minimalPrimes_of_bijOn_comap_pair {A C : Type u} [CommRing A]
    [Nontrivial A] [CommRing C] (left right comp : A →+* C)
    (hbij : Set.BijOn (fun q : Ideal C => (q.comap left, q.comap right))
      (minimalPrimes C) (minimalPrimes A ×ˢ minimalPrimes A))
    (hflat : comp.Flat)
    (hleft : ∀ q ∈ minimalPrimes C, q.comap left ≤ q.comap comp)
    (hright : ∀ q ∈ minimalPrimes C, q.comap right ≤ q.comap comp) :
    ∃! p : Ideal A, p ∈ minimalPrimes A :=
  existsUnique_minimalPrimes_of_comap_comparable left right comp hbij hflat
    (fun q hq => .inl (hleft q hq)) fun q hq => .inl (hright q hq)

/-- If a minimal prime `q` of `C` is the smallest prime containing the images of its contractions
along `l` and `r`, and `s` retracts `l` and `comp` and kills `r` of the maximal ideal, then the
contraction of `q` along `comp` lies in its contraction along `l`. -/
private theorem comap_comp_le_comap_of_retraction {A C : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    [CommRing C] (l r comp : A →+* C) (s : C →+* A) {q : Ideal C} (hq : q ∈ minimalPrimes C)
    (hsmallest : ∀ P : Ideal C, P.IsPrime → (q.comap l).map l ≤ P → (q.comap r).map r ≤ P →
      q ≤ P)
    (hs_comp : s.comp comp = RingHom.id A) (hs_l : s.comp l = RingHom.id A)
    (hs_r : ∀ x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A, s (r x) = 0) :
    q.comap comp ≤ q.comap l := by
  have : q.IsPrime := hq.1.1
  have hq_le : q ≤ (q.comap l).comap s := by
    refine hsmallest _ (Ideal.comap_isPrime s _) ?_ ?_
    · refine Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun x hx => ?_
      simpa [← RingHom.comp_apply, hs_l] using hx
    · refine Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun x hx => ?_
      have : s (r x) = 0 := hs_r x (IsLocalRing.le_maximalIdeal (Ideal.comap_isPrime r q).ne_top hx)
      simp [Ideal.mem_comap, this]
  have := Ideal.comap_mono (f := comp) hq_le
  rwa [Ideal.comap_comap, hs_comp, Ideal.comap_id] at this

/-- **The closing move of Stacks 06E4, from the two identity sections.** Let `left`, `right`,
`comp : A →+* C` be ring maps out of a local ring such that contracting along `left` and along
`right` is a bijection from the minimal primes of `C` to the pairs of minimal primes of `A`, and
each minimal prime of `C` is the smallest prime of `C` containing the images of its two
contractions.  Suppose `comp` is flat and there are retractions `fst`, `snd : C →+* A` with
`fst ∘ left = fst ∘ comp = id` and `snd ∘ right = snd ∘ comp = id`, whose two remaining
composites `fst ∘ right` and `snd ∘ left` vanish on the maximal ideal.  Then `A` has a unique
minimal prime.

For minimal primes `p`, `p'` of `A` let `q` be the minimal prime of `C` they match.  The
contraction `fst⁻¹(p)` is a prime of `C` containing the image of `p` under `left`, because `fst`
undoes `left`, and the image of `p'` under `right`, because `p'` lies in the maximal ideal, which
`fst ∘ right` kills; so it contains `q`.  Contracting along `comp` and using that `fst` undoes
`comp` gives `comp⁻¹(q) ≤ p`, and symmetrically `comp⁻¹(q) ≤ p'`.  Flatness makes `comp⁻¹(q)` a
minimal prime, so it is both `p` and `p'`. -/
theorem existsUnique_minimalPrimes_of_retraction_of_bijOn_comap_pair {A C : Type u}
    [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [CommRing C] (left right comp : A →+* C) (fst snd : C →+* A)
    (hbij : Set.BijOn (fun q : Ideal C => (q.comap left, q.comap right))
      (minimalPrimes C) (minimalPrimes A ×ˢ minimalPrimes A))
    (hsmallest : ∀ q ∈ minimalPrimes C, ∀ P : Ideal C, P.IsPrime →
      (q.comap left).map left ≤ P → (q.comap right).map right ≤ P → q ≤ P)
    (hflat : comp.Flat)
    (hfst_comp : fst.comp comp = RingHom.id A) (hfst_left : fst.comp left = RingHom.id A)
    (hfst_right : ∀ x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A, fst (right x) = 0)
    (hsnd_comp : snd.comp comp = RingHom.id A) (hsnd_right : snd.comp right = RingHom.id A)
    (hsnd_left : ∀ x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A, snd (left x) = 0) :
    ∃! p : Ideal A, p ∈ minimalPrimes A :=
  existsUnique_minimalPrimes_of_comap_comparable left right comp hbij hflat
    (fun q hq => .inr (comap_comp_le_comap_of_retraction left right comp fst hq
      (hsmallest q hq) hfst_comp hfst_left hfst_right))
    fun q hq => .inr (comap_comp_le_comap_of_retraction right left comp snd hq
      (fun P hP h₁ h₂ => hsmallest q hq P hP h₂ h₁) hsnd_comp hsnd_right hsnd_left)


/-- **The local computation of Stacks 06E4.** Let `k` be an algebraically closed field, let `A`
be a strictly henselian local `k`-algebra whose maximal ideal is the kernel of a `k`-algebra
retraction `res`, let `R` be the localization of `A ⊗[k] A` at the maximal ideal cut out by
`res` on both factors, and let `C` be a strict henselization of `R`.  Write `left` and `right`
for the two composites `A → A ⊗[k] A → R → C`.  If a flat ring map `comp : A →+* C` admits two
retractions `fst`, `snd` undoing `comp` together with `left` respectively `right`, the two
remaining composites `fst ∘ right` and `snd ∘ left` killing the maximal ideal, then `A` has a
unique minimal prime.

The pairs of minimal primes of `A` are classified by the minimal primes of `C` (Tag 06DU), each
of which is generated by the images of its two contractions, so the retractions compare the
contraction of `comp` with both members of a pair. -/
theorem existsUnique_minimalPrimes_of_compositionLaw_strictHenselization
    (k A : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    [CommRing A] [Algebra k A] [HenselianLocalRing A]
    [IsSepClosed (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A)]
    (res : A →ₐ[k] k)
    (hres : RingHom.ker res.toRingHom = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
    (R C : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [CommRing C] [IsLocalRing C]
    [Algebra (A ⊗[k] A) R]
    [IsLocalization
      (Submonoid.comap
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.lift res res (fun _ _ ↦ Commute.all _ _)).toRingHom
        (nonZeroDivisors k)) R]
    [Algebra R C]
    (ksep : Type v) [Field ksep] [Algebra (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R) ksep]
    [IsSepClosure (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R) ksep]
    [IsLocalRing.IsHenselization R ksep C]
    (left right comp : A →+* C) (fst snd : C →+* A)
    (hleft : left = (algebraMap R C).comp ((algebraMap (A ⊗[k] A) R).comp
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeft : A →ₐ[k] A ⊗[k] A).toRingHom))
    (hright : right = (algebraMap R C).comp ((algebraMap (A ⊗[k] A) R).comp
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : A →ₐ[k] A ⊗[k] A).toRingHom))
    (hflat : comp.Flat)
    (hfst_comp : fst.comp comp = RingHom.id A) (hfst_left : fst.comp left = RingHom.id A)
    (hfst_right : ∀ x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A, fst (right x) = 0)
    (hsnd_comp : snd.comp comp = RingHom.id A) (hsnd_right : snd.comp right = RingHom.id A)
    (hsnd_left : ∀ x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A, snd (left x) = 0) :
    ∃! p : Ideal A, p ∈ minimalPrimes A := by
  subst hleft hright
  refine existsUnique_minimalPrimes_of_retraction_of_bijOn_comap_pair _ _ comp fst snd
    (minimalPrimes_strictHenselization_tensorProduct_bijOn k A A res res hres hres R C ksep)
    (fun q hq P hP h₁ h₂ => ?_) hflat hfst_comp hfst_left hfst_right hsnd_comp hsnd_right
    hsnd_left
  rw [minimalPrimes_localized_tensorProduct_eq_sup k A A res res hres hres R C ksep q hq]
  exact sup_le h₁ h₂

/-- **The local computation of Stacks 06E4, from a henselization of the base square.** In the
situation of `StacksDraft.existsUnique_minimalPrimes_of_compositionLaw_strictHenselization`,
suppose that `A` is ind-étale over a local `k`-algebra `B` — for instance a strict henselization
of `B` — and that `C` is a henselization, with the same residue field, of the localization `R₀`
of `B ⊗[k] B` at a prime compatible with the one defining `R`.  Then `A` still has a unique
minimal prime.

This is the form in which the computation applies to an algebraic space: `B` is the local ring
of an étale chart and `C` the étale local ring of the chart's self-product, so the henselization
hypothesis is available on `R₀` rather than on `R`.  The two are interchangeable because `R` is
ind-étale over `R₀`. -/
theorem existsUnique_minimalPrimes_of_compositionLaw_indEtale_base
    (k B A : Type u) [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    [CommRing B] [Algebra k B]
    [CommRing A] [Algebra k A] [HenselianLocalRing A]
    [IsSepClosed (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A)]
    [Algebra B A] [IsScalarTower k B A]
    (res : A →ₐ[k] k)
    (hres : RingHom.ker res.toRingHom = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
    (𝔭₀ : Ideal (B ⊗[k] B)) [𝔭₀.IsPrime]
    (R₀ R C : Type u)
    [CommRing R₀] [IsLocalRing R₀] [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [CommRing C] [IsLocalRing C]
    [Algebra (B ⊗[k] B) R₀] [IsLocalization.AtPrime R₀ 𝔭₀]
    [Algebra (A ⊗[k] A) R]
    [IsLocalization
      (Submonoid.comap
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.lift res res (fun _ _ ↦ Commute.all _ _)).toRingHom
        (nonZeroDivisors k)) R]
    [Algebra (B ⊗[k] B) (A ⊗[k] A)] [Algebra R₀ R] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap R₀ R)]
    [Algebra R₀ C] [Algebra R C] [IsScalarTower R₀ R C]
    (ksep : Type v) [Field ksep]
    [Algebra (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R₀) ksep] [Algebra (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R) ksep]
    [IsScalarTower (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R₀) (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R) ksep]
    [IsLocalRing.IsHenselization R₀ ksep C]
    [IsSepClosure (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R) ksep]
    (hmap : ∀ b b' : B, algebraMap (B ⊗[k] B) (A ⊗[k] A) (b ⊗ₜ[k] b') =
      algebraMap B A b ⊗ₜ[k] algebraMap B A b')
    (hsq : (algebraMap R₀ R).comp (algebraMap (B ⊗[k] B) R₀) =
      (algebraMap (A ⊗[k] A) R).comp (algebraMap (B ⊗[k] B) (A ⊗[k] A)))
    (hind : IndEtale B A)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective
      (algebraMap (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R₀) (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R)))
    (left right comp : A →+* C) (fst snd : C →+* A)
    (hleft : left = (algebraMap R C).comp ((algebraMap (A ⊗[k] A) R).comp
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeft : A →ₐ[k] A ⊗[k] A).toRingHom))
    (hright : right = (algebraMap R C).comp ((algebraMap (A ⊗[k] A) R).comp
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : A →ₐ[k] A ⊗[k] A).toRingHom))
    (hflat : comp.Flat)
    (hfst_comp : fst.comp comp = RingHom.id A) (hfst_left : fst.comp left = RingHom.id A)
    (hfst_right : ∀ x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A, fst (right x) = 0)
    (hsnd_comp : snd.comp comp = RingHom.id A) (hsnd_right : snd.comp right = RingHom.id A)
    (hsnd_left : ∀ x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A, snd (left x) = 0) :
    ∃! p : Ideal A, p ∈ minimalPrimes A := by
  set f := (Algebra.TensorProduct.lift res res (fun _ _ ↦ Commute.all _ _)).toRingHom with hf
  have h𝔭 : (RingHom.ker f).IsPrime := RingHom.ker_isPrime f
  have hcomap : Submonoid.comap f (nonZeroDivisors k) = (RingHom.ker f).primeCompl :=
    comap_nonZeroDivisors_eq_primeCompl f (RingHom.ker f) rfl
  have hatprime : IsLocalization (RingHom.ker f).primeCompl R := by
    rw [← hcomap]
    infer_instance
  have : IsLocalRing.IsHenselization R ksep C :=
    isHenselization_localizedTensorProduct k B A 𝔭₀ (RingHom.ker f) R₀ R C ksep hmap hsq hind
      hsurj
  exact existsUnique_minimalPrimes_of_compositionLaw_strictHenselization k A res hres R C ksep
    left right comp fst snd hleft hright hflat hfst_comp hfst_left hfst_right hsnd_comp
    hsnd_right hsnd_left

end StacksDraft

end
